#!/bin/sh
#
# config.sh for perl 5.42.3 on wasm32-wasip1, written by hand.
#
# Configure never probes this target. scripts/20_target.sh copies this file into a fresh tree,
# fills in the @ROOT@, @BUILD@, @SDK@, @SYSROOT@, @NATIVE@ and @NATIVEPERL@ paths, and runs
# "sh ./Configure -S", which only substitutes these values into config.h, Makefile and the
# other .SH files.
#
# Each d_* function symbol says whether wasi-libc in wasi-sdk 34 both declares the function
# (under -std=c99 -D_GNU_SOURCE) and defines it in libc.a or a linked emulation library.
# Processes, signals, users and groups, sockets, SysV IPC and dynamic loading are undefined
# whatever wasi-libc declares: WASI preview1 has none of them.
#
# Every core XS extension that can work under WASI is in static_ext and linked into perl;
# the generated perlmain.c registers each. Encode's sub-extensions are listed as Configure
# lists them for a static Encode. Left out: threads and threads/shared (no threads), IPC/SysV
# (no System V IPC), Sys/Syslog (no syslog), DB_File, GDBM_File, NDBM_File and ODBM_File
# (their C libraries are not built), PerlIO/mmap (wasi-libc's mmap only copies a file into
# memory), and XS/APItest and XS/Typemap (test scaffolding perl never installs).
# The pure-Perl Thread/Queue and Thread/Semaphore are left out of nonxs_ext with threads: both
# load threads::shared.
#
# d_clock, d_clock_getres, d_clock_gettime and d_clock_nanosleep are not Configure variables:
# Time::HiRes reads them, when present, instead of running probe programs on the build host.
# cppsymbols is what the pinned clang predefines for wasm32-wasip1 with the -D flags every
# compile gets (clang -dM -E of an empty file, as NAME=value, spaces escaped, sorted).
# i_sysun is undefined because wasi-libc's struct sockaddr_un has no sun_path.
# -Werror=int-conversion: a pointer used as an integer, or the reverse, traps on wasm32 when it
# goes wrong, so it never builds. (wasi-libc's clockid_t is a pointer; Time::HiRes gets integer
# clock ids from include/wasi-perl-posix.h instead.)
#
# Package name      : perl5
# Source directory  : .
# Target system     : wasi preview1 wasm32
#

